sentences.l:
And of men, no living mortal, not even one in the full bloom of youth,
easily could shift it, since a great sign has been wrought
in the artfully-fashioned bed;

For always, to me, my heart in my dear breast
shuddered lest some one of mortals should deceive me with words,
coming;

And as when welcome land appears to swimmers,
whose well-made ship Poseidon on the open-sea
shatters, pressed hard by wind and strong-packed wave;

and few escape the grey sea to the mainland,
swimming, and much about the skin the brine has caked,
and glad they step on the land, having escaped misfortune;

“A couch, indeed, for you will be then, whenever in your own
heart you wish, since the gods caused you to arrive
at your well-built home and your own fatherland;

to go off home, and to offer sacred hecatombs
to the immortal gods, who hold the wide sky,
to all, quite in order, one after another;

and death for me myself out of the salt-sea,
very mild, of such a kind, will come, that shall slay me
under sleek old age, worn down;
